  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing tropical deforestation and degradation with journalism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims the to increase the knowledge of deforestation of tropical forest and the effects that deforestation may have on climate change through quality journalism. Furthermore, the project also intend to contribute to an informed global dialogue on bio-diversity. The project includes three parts:
Project 1 - Informing global dialogue on tropical forests through news reporting
Project 2 - Addressing hidden drivers of deforestation with investigative reporting
Project 3 - Mongabay GeoJournalism Lab: research communication for accountability
The project intend to contribute to increase knowledge on both issues of climate change mitigation and climate change adaption. The project focus on Indonesia, Brasil, Bolivia, Peru, and Colombia, and the countries in the Congo Basin.</narrative>
  </description>
